===Brazil vs Spain===
Spain had control of the game in the first half and took the lead 10 minutes before halftime when [[Adelardo Rodríguez|Adelardo]] shot into the bottom corner from twenty meters. At the beginning of the second half [[Nílton Santos]] committed a foul inside the penalty area but the referee being far away from the episode awarded only a free kick to the Spanish team.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20130118094312/http://www.v-brazil.com/world-cup/history/1962-Chile.php Brazil in the World Cup 1962]</ref> Spain also had a goal disallowed for no evident reason. In the last 15 minutes of the game [[Amarildo Tavares da Silveira|Amarildo]] (who was replacing Pele after the latter was injured in the previous match) scored twice to complete the Brazilian comeback.<ref>{{usurped|1=[https://web.archive.org/web/20170509015505/http://www.linguasport.com/futbol/internacional/mundial/1962_CHILE_FS.htm World Cup 1962 Final Stage: Game Details]}}</ref><ref>[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mAjoYQoboPs Brazil vs Spain on YouTube]</ref>

